orward to the next objective", 'medium': 'FIRST Mewtwo — the strongest Pokemon in the game, at the bottom of Cerulean Cave. The guard only steps aside for the Champion, and the Master Ball has been waiting for exactly this moment — the gym comes right after; that errand is the road', 'long': 'Enjoy the post-game as Champion (Cerulean Cave, the Pokédex)'}, 'strategy': "1) QUARTERMASTER: the bag is thin — 0 potion(s), 1 status cure(s), 0 revive(s), $29260 in pocket. Money is ammo: next Mart, stock potions toward ~12, cures for what's been hurting the team, a couple of Revives. Never walk into a gym or a long route under-stocked.\n2) DEX PUSH: 20/50 species caught — at 50 the Route 15 aide (by Fuchsia) hands over the EXP. SHARE (the whole bench levels off every fight). Catch every NEW species you cross; never wander just to hunt.\n3) STANDING ORDERS: the goal is ROLL CREDITS. Forward progress beats wandering; heal beats fighting hurt; type advantage decides fights; build the planned team, not just the ace."} options=['battle', 'wander_catch', 'talk_npc', 'travel:3,19', 'travel:3,39', 'travel:3,20', 'travel:3,21']

